cff-version: 1.2.0
type: software
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "FedBagSafe: Official PyTorch Framework for Byzantine-Robust and Privacy-Preserving Personalized Federated Learning"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-23"
abstract: >-
  FedBagSafe is an open-source PyTorch framework created and maintained by
  Seyed Saeed Razavi for Byzantine-robust, privacy-preserving, and personalized
  federated learning under non-IID data. It is the official implementation of
  the FedBagSafe article in Computers and Electrical Engineering, which builds
  on the design of LightFedSelect (Razavi et al., IEEE ICCKE 2025, DOI:
  10.1109/ICCKE68588.2025.11273877). The framework provides server-side bagged
  multi-aggregation, client-side accuracy-over-loss selection, adaptive
  fail-safe rollback, and optional TenSEAL CKKS homomorphic encryption across
  CIFAR-10, CIFAR-100, FashionMNIST, and FEMNIST.
